abstract: >-
  Preregistered audit of how the uncertainty reported on the robomimic Multi-Human benchmarks
  decomposes into training seed, demonstration resampling, operator composition, and rollout
  noise. Contains the preregistration with dated amendments, the pinned environment, immutable
  partition files, fixed evaluation initial conditions, the training and evaluation queues,
  per-run and per-rollout results for 138 BC-RNN runs (6,900 rollouts) and a 500-rollout
  re-evaluation of 46 Square checkpoints (23,000 rollouts), and the scripts that regenerate
  every number, table and figure in the accompanying paper.
